{"id": "2026-10-14-news-russia-pounds-ukraine-s-grid-despite-ceasefire", "date": "2026-10-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russia pounds Ukraine's grid despite 'ceasefire'", "summary": "A massive Russian missile and drone strike on Ukraine's energy system on 13-14 October killed at least six and cut power to over half a million, two days after Trump's unconfirmed 'energy ceasefire'.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/14/massive-russian-attack-on-ukraine-kills-at-least-six-cuts-power-in-kyiv", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Russia launched a massive missile and drone attack on Ukraine's power grid from the evening of Tuesday 13 October into Wednesday 14 October, two days after US President Donald Trump announced an \"energy ceasefire\" that Moscow never confirmed. Ukraine's Air Force counted 39 missiles, most of them on ballistic trajectories, and 128 drones. It said it downed four ballistic missiles and 115 drones, and recorded hits at 22 locations. Russia's Defence Ministry said it struck two power-and-heating plants in Kyiv, two more in the surrounding region, a substation, a heating plant in Kharkiv and a data centre in Kyiv. Al Jazeera counted at least six people killed across the country, three of them in Kyiv. More than half a million people lost power. President Volodymyr Zelensky called it a deliberate strike on \"the very infrastructure covered by the ceasefire announced by the American President\". He said partners gave no early warning of the ballistic launches. His Air Force spokesperson later said warnings did come for three later waves, but not the first. Zelensky also told NPR that Washington had threatened to cut intelligence sharing unless Ukraine stopped drone strikes on Russian refineries.", "why": "Trump announced the \"energy ceasefire\" on 11 October without either side confirming it, and the heaviest strike on Ukraine's energy system this autumn has now tested it. Kyiv also says US pressure is limiting its own long-range strikes.", "thread_id": "2026-10-14-news-russia-pounds-ukraine-s-grid-despite-ceasefire", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-14", "event_date": "2026-10-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Kyiv", "Volodymyr Zelensky", "Donald Trump"]}
{"id": "2026-10-14-news-pope-leo-xiv-operated-on-for-lung-cancer", "date": "2026-10-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Pope Leo XIV operated on for lung cancer", "summary": "The Holy See said surgeons removed the lower lobe of Pope Leo XIV's right lung on 13 October and confirmed lung adenocarcinoma.", "url": "https://www.vaticannews.va/en/pope/news/2026-10/pope-leo-surgery-gemelli-hospital-successful.html", "source_domain": "vaticannews.va", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["world", "health"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Pope Leo XIV, 71, had the lower lobe of his right lung removed at Rome's Gemelli Hospital on Tuesday 13 October, and tissue examined during the operation confirmed lung adenocarcinoma, the Holy See Press Office said. Adenocarcinoma is the most common form of lung cancer. The surgeons said the video-assisted operation, a keyhole technique, lasted about 90 minutes and had no complications. They removed the whole lobe \"to ensure a radical resection\", meaning to take out all the tumour with a margin. Further tests on the removed tissue will follow in the coming days. The planned one-week hospital stay is unchanged. On Wednesday morning the Press Office said the Pope had a calm night and promised more information later in the day.", "why": "the doctors have not yet said what stage the cancer is or whether more treatment is needed. Those post-operative results will decide how long the head of the world's 1.4 billion Catholics is kept from his duties.", "thread_id": "2026-10-14-news-pope-leo-xiv-operated-on-for-lung-cancer", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-14", "event_date": "2026-10-13", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Pope Leo XIV", "Holy See", "Gemelli Hospital"]}
{"id": "2026-10-14-news-bank-of-america-hit-with-record-us-penalties", "date": "2026-10-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Bank of America hit with record US penalties", "summary": "The US Treasury announced over $1.21 billion in penalties against Bank of America for anti-money-laundering and sanctions violations on 13 October.", "url": "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0657", "source_domain": "home.treasury.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The US Treasury announced more than $1.21 billion in penalties against Bank of America on Tuesday 13 October for anti-money-laundering and sanctions violations, the third-largest penalty in Treasury history. FinCEN, the Treasury's financial-intelligence unit, assessed $1.2 billion. Bank of America admitted it wilfully violated the Bank Secrecy Act and failed to report more than $5 billion in suspicious transactions on time. More than $1 billion of that was linked to Chinese money-laundering networks, fraud and possible trade-based laundering tied to the US–Mexico border. The bank regulator OCC added a $750 million penalty, its largest ever. The release does not explain how that amount fits within the $1.21 billion total. OFAC, the Treasury's sanctions office, settled 475 apparent sanctions violations involving Russia, Iran and other programmes for $11.6 million. The bank told AFP it has invested billions in financial-crime controls.", "why": "the US regulators say the second-largest US bank left much of its suspicious-activity detection to law enforcement and other banks for years. This is the same compliance failing that has cost Swiss banks dearly in US enforcement.", "thread_id": "2026-10-14-news-bank-of-america-hit-with-record-us-penalties", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-14", "event_date": "2026-10-13", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Bank of America", "US Treasury", "FinCEN", "OCC", "OFAC"]}
{"id": "2026-10-14-news-turkey-seizes-opposition-broadcaster-halk-tv", "date": "2026-10-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Turkey seizes opposition broadcaster Halk TV", "summary": "Turkish police took over Halk TV, the main private opposition channel, on 14 October and placed it under a state-appointed administrator.", "url": "https://www.rfi.fr/fr/europe/20261014-turquie-le-pouvoir-prend-le-contr%C3%B4le-de-la-principale-t%C3%A9l%C3%A9vision-de-l-opposition", "source_domain": "rfi.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Turkish police took over the Istanbul headquarters of Halk TV, the country's main private opposition television channel, early on Wednesday 14 October, and the channel was placed under a state-appointed administrator. The Istanbul prosecutor's office said arrest warrants were issued for 17 people and 11 were detained in simultaneous operations. Management of the channel was handed to the Savings Deposit Insurance Fund (TMSF), a public body Ankara uses to run seized companies. The channel said its live broadcast was cut off. Staff were kept out of the building after the raid began at about 05:30 local time. The Journalists' Union of Turkey says 17 journalists are currently in detention.", "why": "Halk TV follows the pro-opposition Tele 1, which was placed under the same kind of administration earlier, so Turkey's main critical broadcasters are now under state-appointed control.", "thread_id": "2026-10-14-news-turkey-seizes-opposition-broadcaster-halk-tv", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-14", "event_date": "2026-10-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Turkey", "Halk TV", "TMSF"]}
{"id": "2026-10-14-news-bern-moves-to-give-disabled-adults-the-vote", "date": "2026-10-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Bern moves to give disabled adults the vote", "summary": "The Federal Council opened a consultation on a constitutional amendment ending the exclusion of adults with intellectual disabilities from federal political rights.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/E7kYfiMOZOmH", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Federal Council on Wednesday 14 October opened a consultation on amending the Constitution so that adults with intellectual disabilities are no longer barred from voting in federal matters. Today, people under a general guardianship (curatelle de portée générale) or a mandate for incapacity on grounds of lasting incapacity of judgement lose their federal political rights. The change to Art. 136 of the Constitution and the federal political-rights laws would let them vote in National Council elections and federal votes, and sign initiatives and referendums. Parliament asked for the change in motion 24.4266. Several cantons have already dropped equivalent rules. The consultation runs until 28 January 2027. Because it changes the Constitution, the reform will need a mandatory vote of people and cantons.", "why": "it would end one of the last categorical exclusions from the Swiss vote. It is part of a wider overhaul of adult-protection law that aims to abolish general guardianship.", "thread_id": "2026-10-14-news-bern-moves-to-give-disabled-adults-the-vote", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-14", "event_date": "2026-10-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council", "Swiss Constitution"]}
{"id": "2026-10-14-news-swiss-money-laundering-risk-map-flags-crypto", "date": "2026-10-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss money-laundering risk map flags crypto", "summary": "Switzerland's third national money-laundering and terrorist-financing risk assessment finds exposure stable but flags crypto banks, fintech and wealth management as high risk.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/Amio6afANTmb", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Federal Council on Wednesday 14 October received Switzerland's third national assessment of money-laundering and terrorist-financing risks, which finds overall exposure stable since 2021 but flags crypto, fintech and wealth management as high-risk. The report comes from the federal interdepartmental coordinating group on money laundering (GCBF). It names organised crime, corruption, property crime and tax offences as the main threats, mostly with an international dimension. It places the highest residual risks in wealth-management banks and \"other banks\", especially crypto banks. It also rates as high risk fintech firms, virtual-asset service providers, money transmitters, trustees, legal advisers, fiduciary companies and real estate. \"Residual\" risk means the risk left after existing controls. It recommends more resources for supervisors and prosecutors, better databases, and a review of how well the reporting system, precious-metals controls and the new transparency register work.", "why": "it is the official map of where Swiss authorities think dirty money gets in, and it comes a day after the US fined Bank of America over the same kind of failings (see World).", "thread_id": "2026-10-14-news-swiss-money-laundering-risk-map-flags-crypto", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-14", "event_date": "2026-10-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council", "GCBF", "FINMA"]}
{"id": "2026-10-14-news-poll-swiss-reject-vat-hike-for-ahv", "date": "2026-10-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Poll: Swiss reject VAT hike for AHV", "summary": "A Leewas poll published 14 October shows the VAT rise for the 13th AHV pension rejected 60-36 ahead of the 29 November vote, with only the fireworks initiative clearly ahead.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/un-mois-avant-les-votations-les-suisses-sont-divises-sur-la-tva-le-materiel-de-guerre-et-le-mariage-mais-unis-contre-les-feux-d-artifice", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A Leewas poll published on Wednesday 14 October finds three of the four federal proposals on the 29 November ballot heading for defeat, including the VAT increase to fund the 13th AHV/AVS pension payment, rejected 60% to 36%. Only SP/PS voters are split on the VAT rise (49% yes, 45% no), and about 80% of SVP/UDC voters oppose it. The change to the War Material Act, which would loosen arms-export rules, is the closest: 47% no, 44% yes, 9% undecided. Men back it and women oppose it. The Centre party's initiative on federal taxation of married couples trails 38% to 51%. Only the initiative to limit fireworks has a clear majority, 68% to 30% in the detailed figures (Le Temps' summary gives 65%). The poll surveyed 11,239 people on 7–8 October, with a margin of error of 1.6 points. Leewas notes high \"rather yes/rather no\" shares, meaning opinion is still forming.", "why": "this is the first wave of polling. The pension-funding vote decides how the 13th pension payment voters approved is paid for.", "thread_id": "2026-10-14-news-poll-swiss-reject-vat-hike-for-ahv", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-14", "event_date": "2026-11-29", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Leewas", "AHV", "War Material Act"]}
{"id": "2026-10-14-news-reporting-duty-for-medical-device-shortages", "date": "2026-10-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Reporting duty for medical device shortages", "summary": "The Federal Council opened a consultation requiring firms to report shortages of vital medical devices to FONES from August 2027.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/CjMfSkioYMfq", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "health"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Federal Council on Wednesday 14 October opened a consultation to make companies report shortages and stock-outs of vital medical devices to the Federal Office for National Economic Supply (FONES/OFAE), as they already must for vital medicines. \"Vital\" means devices whose absence directly endangers patients' lives or has serious health consequences. The national economic-supply organisation will name which products are covered. Reports will go through the existing electronic Therapeutic Products Platform. The consultation runs until 28 January 2027, and the duty is planned to start on 1 August 2027.", "why": "supply disruptions have multiplied in recent years. Without the reports, Bern has no overall picture from which to decide on emergency measures such as releasing stocks.", "thread_id": "2026-10-14-news-reporting-duty-for-medical-device-shortages", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-14", "event_date": "2026-10-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council", "FONES"]}
{"id": "2026-10-14-news-insurers-investment-income-stays-optional", "date": "2026-10-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Insurers' investment income stays optional", "summary": "The Federal Council said health insurers need not use all capital income to lower premiums, keeping the voluntary mechanism.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/k9VijbvpdXiJ", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "health"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Federal Council said on Wednesday 14 October that health insurers should not be required to put all their investment income towards lowering premiums, and that the current voluntary mechanism is enough. In its report answering postulate 22.3930 (Feller), it says insurers may already deduct a share of capital income from the costs charged to basic insurance, and most do when their solvency is good. Keeping it voluntary avoids extra premium swings and lets insurers use the income to build reserves when needed.", "why": "for policyholders facing another premium rise, the government has declined to make insurers' investment income a guaranteed source of premium relief. How much relief there is still depends on each insurer's choices.", "thread_id": "2026-10-14-news-insurers-investment-income-stays-optional", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-14", "event_date": "2026-10-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council"]}
